{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>An old plague of tzara'at.</b> Here Rashi z\"l did not examine with full precision, and in Torat Kohanim it concludes: white hair is a sign of impurity, and raw flesh is a sign of impurity — this teaches that raw flesh impurifies without having turned. And this we derive from what is written ״הוא״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:04.986932720Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}